WEBVTT

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.130
Grandfather,

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.170
I will come back.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.610
Looks like a prison photo...

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.760
Hey, guys, please smile.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.570
This is going to be important propaganda for Section III.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.960
Try to imagine all the readers looking at the front page.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.950
Your image is what's important, your image.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:49.770
Please give us your best smile.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.540
Ah, oh well.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.520
Cheese!

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.480
They say we're easy-going and whatnot,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.560
but we're quite busy ourselves, too.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.710
If the interview begins to interfere with our operations,

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.190
then the interview ends there.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.460
Umm...

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.560
Die Welt Newspaper,
Note: "Die Welt" means "The World" in German

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.340
I'm Dalton from the social welfare section.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.790
I completely understand what you mean.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.000
It is not our intention to interfere with your work.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.510
This article is part of a series called "Now, After Reconstruction",

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.560
and we would like to inform the public of the activities that Section III does.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.710
So, it's finally time for my face
to make a nation-wide debut, huh?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.450
That photo we just took, it's going to appear in this paper.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.140
It is a national paper after all.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.760
And who was the one that didn't want the interview?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.070
I was...

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.580
...because I still believe we're just a money-collecting machine for the government.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.090
But if our photo is going to be in it,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.510
then it's a whole different story.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.730
"Easy-going," indeed.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.330
We look forward to working with you today.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.080
Same here, 2nd Lieutenant.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.600
About that "image" you just mentioned,

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.500
I thought that was a great word.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.210
That was a great word?

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.430
To imagine the future of this country after all the war relief.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.820
In other words, after all the reconstruction has been completed,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.870
to imagine a day where everyone can lead a steady life.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.970
I am imagining the day when
Section III can finally accomplish that goal.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:15.960
The day when you can accomplish your goal, eh?

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:20.110
Of course, I am proud of Section III.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.610
But as long as Section III stays busy,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.740
one cannot say the rebuilding of the Empire has been completed.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.420
The smiles that we see on our missions...

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.160
...are like medals of honor for us.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.710
A future where this country will be filled with smiles...

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.080
If people can imagine a prosperous future where people aren't prejudiced by their personal interests...

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.160
...but instead have their own dreams to pursue...

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.500
...then the war relief will be expedited.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.800
And that's a direct message to the readers, right?

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:53.270
Then, everyone, please give me comments one by one about your efforts in Section III.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.390
What exactly is he expecting us to say after hearing such hot-blooded words?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.170
Dr. Colt?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.260
Are you there?

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.660
Who are you?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.810
You, again?

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.840
What is it this time?

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.130
What do you want to know about tanks?

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.070
I saw this thing today.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:31.560
Were there prototypes left behind in the army?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.340
No, a soldier had this on him.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.350
In fact, he had it right here, in a holster.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.740
Really?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.990
From our last interview,

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:44.600
you talked about the absolute
point-blank range attack, right, Doctor?

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:50.280
You also said that it was so unrealistic that the project fell apart altogether.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:54.100
But, today, I've seen it.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:58.730
Thanks for your help, guys.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.030
Ah, no problem.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.130
Nice work, Mr. Dalton.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.460
Heading home now?

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.470
Yes, although we can only sleep after we head back to the dormitory.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.290
We have our meals and showers here.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.020
That's a mighty big gun you got there.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.540
Yeah, I mean, look at the size of this guy.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.710
That's why a normal gun would be like a toy to him.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.120
It's a custom-made gun.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.080
That's all there is to it.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.940
I only caught a slight glimpse of it,

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.620
but I believe it has been used frequently.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.420
Section III has visited me once before.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.100
Someone did express interest in the Door Knocker.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.920
They should know the meaning of that gun.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.580
I don't have any evidence,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.640
but they appeared to run away from the subject.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.910
Was the absolute point-blank range project really abandoned?

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.410
Perhaps there's something that even you don't know, Doctor.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.310
Are you going to put this in an article?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.650
Someday.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.720
That's why I came to you, Doctor.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.180
Please tell me the specifics again...

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.800
...about the Door Knocker.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.160
Then, could you tell me more about
the man who possessed the Door Knocker?

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.570
Yo, big man.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.440
Ah, morning.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.720
What's going on, getting together this early?

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:39.160
Note: "Drei Teile Bericht" means "Three Part Feature" in German

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.680
This is you, right?
Note: "Drei Teile Bericht" means "Three Part Feature" in German

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.640
Yeah...

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.060
I knew it.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.810
You've got a really commendable job, my man.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.810
Is there anything we can do for you?

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.160
Anything, just tell us.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:54.280
And that blonde girl said some good things, too.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:08:00.490
When I was young, I used to imagine a prosperous future, too.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:02.910
If there were more of you guys,

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:06.410
this country might get a bit better.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.470
Good morning, my fellow comrades.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.510
You're early today.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.960
I looked the best on the photo, right?

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.830
We can't tell because it's too small.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.790
I wonder what kind of feedback it'll get.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:25.320
Everyone's supporting Section III.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:25.940
Everyone?

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:27.590
My neighbors...

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.980
They were especially touched by the Lieutenant's words.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.530
I see.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.520
To imagine the future...

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.700
It's a small thing...

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.310
But I think it's a big war relief.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:45.420
Hey Cecile.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.290
Two bottles of beer, please.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.660
Pay up first.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.800
Just put it on my tab.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.110
It's way overdue.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:52.340
The master's going to get mad at me.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.010
Aww, come on, don't say that.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.260
What're you reading?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.560
This.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.410
Ah, I read that, too.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:08:59.970
What about it?

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.860
I saw this person before.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.140
I see her a lot at the cemetery.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:06.940
Ain't she a noble?

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.220
She's from the Malvin family,
one of the Thirteen Appointed Families.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.650
Such bullshit.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.400
"We're working hard on war relief"
is just the excuse of the higher-ups, right?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.570
And for her, that's just a noble's way of self-satisfaction; it's just a game for her.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.620
I am friggin' pissed at that article.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.460
This is what I thought...

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.080
What?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.880
I've finally found a way to use my brother's manuscript.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.560
Manuscript? That one?

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.470
Sorry, I can't figure out what you're trying to say.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.300
Good morning, dearest Alice.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:50.200
Good morning, Lord Schultz.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.890
Alice, please wait!

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:58.080
I am deeply moved by yesterday's article!

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:03.230
You are the most beautiful when
you are doing your job at Section III.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.200
At least, allow me to apologize for my earlier rudeness.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.460
Let me give you a trip to the army HQ today.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:10.710
I thank you, Lord Schultz.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.200
But, as thankful as I am for your intentions,

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.460
I have decided that I walk there every day.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:38.180
Excuse me, you're 2nd Lieutenant Alice L. Malvin, right?

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.780
Yes.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.210
I've seen you several times at the cemetery.

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.080
Same here.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:49.050
I knew it was you when I saw the photo in the paper.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.290
Quiet!

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.580
I just want you to come with me for one day.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.590
Quite a dangerous way of asking me...

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:07.710
Alice!

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.470
Lord Schultz.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:10.970
What's the meaning of this?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.190
Weren't you going to walk?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.960
This is part of Section III's tasks.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.900
I have to head to the scene now.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.850
These people are cooperating with me in this task.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.610
Wow...

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.340
This is only one part of it.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.480
Everyone's counting on you guys.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.310
More like we didn't get any coverage before.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:38.100
But, this is criticism.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.550
They're calling us the public facade of the government.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.100
Well, it's the truth.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.970
There are some of those in here.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:47.690
I think it's just another way of showing their high expectations.

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:49.890
What's wrong?

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.460
I'm happy...

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:57.570
...that there's so many people supporting the Pumpkin Scissors unit.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:02.960
And so, for the second part of my article,

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:10.480
I was thinking about giving you guys individual spotlights.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.770
For example, Corporal Oland,

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.040
what missions left an impression on you, etc.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.300
Hey, you're that...

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.560
The LT's self-proclaimed fiancé.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.180
What? This person?

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.010
I'm not self-proclaimed!

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:36.150
Eventually I will be!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.030
Please don't get your spit on us.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.310
Calm down.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:40.990
What do you want?

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.410
Was any mission given to Alice today?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.270
No.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:46.260
I knew it.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:47.980
I thought it was strange.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:49.240
Something happened to the lieutenant?

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.910
Some suspicious people...

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:55.210
Don't tell me that was... a kidnapping?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:04.650
I understand.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.660
I won't write about it yet.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.080
I do feel sorry for resorting to violent means.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.850
I just wanted to ask you...

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.060
Why did you come without resistance?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.050
You could've asked for help from that nobleman.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.300
I just wanted to know your intentions.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.660
Even though you might get killed?

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:55.480
You aren't murderers.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.830
Hmm, wanna see?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.070
Stop it.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:01.600
That's not why we brought her here.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.040
But she's a noble and a soldier,

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.540
the types of people we despise the most!

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.690
She's the same type of person that killed your brother!

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:11.950
Killed?

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.250
This was the reason.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.520
My brother was a writer for a small tabloid.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.430
He went around the underground world of the Empire...

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.790
...and wrote about rumors he'd hear there.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.930
That was a scoop that my brother found.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:35.940
There's a scandal that the army you're in is trying to cover up.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.650
But ever since he'd started investigating that scoop,

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:41.990
my brother said there was always someone following him.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.350
What's this scandal about?

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.790
Just listen to me until the end.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.610
That manuscript isn't complete...

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:52.400
...because my brother was killed before it could've been.

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.080
They said he fell into the river from being drunk, man.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.560
It wasn't an accident like that!

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.280
They wanted to shut his mouth, basically.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.950
He was obviously killed by your friends in the army.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.880
Are you saying the army did this?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.660
Because the manuscript disappeared...

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.480
...including all the interview memos...

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.170
And this is...

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.360
A copy.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:13.070
He probably felt his life was in danger,

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.300
so he split it into three parts and hid it.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:17.800
It was like treasure hunting for us.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.100
You want to publish this manuscript, right?

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.840
I believe that was my brother's wish.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:25.730
A manuscript is complete only when it is published.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.260
Using me?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:28.900
Yes.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.950
Why must it be me?

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.070
"Imagine it."

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.890
Those were your words!

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.550
If you want to accomplish that war relief of yours,

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.400
I think you have to start by exposing the ugliness of this country.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:47.070
What exactly can we see
in the future with your whitewash?!

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.750
I know it's whitewash,

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.470
but changing that into reality is our task.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:54.450
This is great.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:55.890
Are you looking at reality?

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.700
Try to look around here.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:00.060
The future that everyone's imagining...

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.090
...is just the food they need for the next few days!

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:03.970
If you want to bring us smiles,

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:07.980
then just fill our stomachs and let us live in warm houses!

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.410
To do that,

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:13.700
you need to change the very core of
the government that ruined our cities!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.170
There's no point in simply polishing the front of it.

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:19.740
Read this...

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:24.250
This manuscript has the power to change the government from the inside.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.720
Invisible 9...

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.700
Looks like you're in shock.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.920
I don't blame you for not knowing,

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.820
but the only reason you could say
those words is because you were ignorant.

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:50.330
Shall we get Mer-kun to follow her scent?

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.520
That's pointless.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.990
They moved by carriage.

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.660
We just found that carriage.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:02.290
Then, can't we start from places where the carriage stopped?

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.990
Right...

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.830
We haven't had any contact from her, either.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:09.960
Then we can only rely on Oreld now.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.840
With all his acquaintances, we could probably find the man and woman that Schultz saw and-

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.080
Yes, it was this one! This carriage!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.470
Where did you find it?

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:21.730
Where's Lady Alice?!

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.470
We still don't know where the LT is.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:28.150
We found this carriage in the South sector of the capital,

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.260
but we couldn't find any clue to the whereabouts of the LT.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.750
I see.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:37.130
I knew I should've have forced her to get onto my carriage back then.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:39.250
I'll go search for her.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.360
Search? Where?

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:42.600
I don't know,

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.850
but we have to.

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.040
I'm sure the lieutenant is waiting for us, too.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:05.770
I didn't expect you to come down to this scrap house personally.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:08.060
You had something to tell me, no?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.110
"That" is what I wanted to tell you about.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.530
Tanks are the most powerful weapons on the face of this planet,

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:20.240
but I didn't expect a foot soldier to exceed their power.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.670
With all the technology the Kauplan Institute possesses,

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:27.000
this sure was a ridiculous thing to do.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:29.110
It was an experiment.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.910
I just strengthened the "shield" and the "spear".

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:35.260
War was the place to advance our technologies.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.950
You know that.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.090
How unpleasant.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:43.850
And exactly how much effect did those soldiers have in the war?

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.580
The war is past tense.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.640
The experiment has reached its next stage.

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:50.650
What?

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.390
The war is over.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:55.800
The way of war is gradually changing.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:00.490
My experiment subject will evolve along with these changes, as well.

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:02.410
What do you mean?

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:05.650
Ah, let me ask some questions, too.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.910
Who was the person that talked to you about my experiment subject?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.130
A reporter from the newspaper.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.500
He called himself Dalton from the Die Welt paper.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:17.650
I thank you, Doctor.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.420
You learned of something you shouldn't have.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.520
Hey, keep watching outside.

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:41.070
I'm starving, man.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:42.490
There's nothing in here.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.040
How are things?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:48.310
Miss Noble read the manuscript and is in shock.

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:53.620
How do you guys want to change the government with this?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.130
You're the one that needs to think about that.

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:57.840
Imagine it.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.330
We don't have any power.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.370
We'll just be killed like my brother.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:06.030
If you really want to carry out war relief,

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:07.460
you need to use any methods...

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:09.590
even if it means tainting yourself...

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.160
even if it means your life...

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.230
you have to do this, right?!

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:16.770
Will you do this? Or not?

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.410
There's also a way to not publish this.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:24.840
We can just tell the higher-ups that we have this manuscript,

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:27.530
and it should be a big enough bomb for them.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.830
That's not going to work!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.830
We need to let the entire country know about this or else it's meaningless!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.920
It would also be meaningless if they don't know whether this is the truth or not.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:37.540
Looks like you're the same as all of those people in the government!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:38.840
You're nothing but talk!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.380
Then aren't the Pumpkin Scissors a war aggravator, too?

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.610
Wastefully giving people hope like that...

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.460
Hope won't fill our stomachs!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:51.040
I only hear what you guys are saying as complaints while using the manuscript as an excuse.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.150
If there's something you want to change,

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.180
you should change it with your own hands!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.880
Just barking without doing anything,

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.510
people's hearts won't be moved.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.810
Shut up...

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.910
Concerning your brother who lost his life before he could accomplish his task,

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:08.220
I wish to express my deepest regrets for him.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:14.680
But you guys are just using this article to quickly find someone to voice your complaints to, no?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.130
Enough of your preaching!!

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.500
You're just scared of the scandal.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.900
You're just a soldier, after all.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.200
You're just trying to protect the army's reputation!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.130
Enough already.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:29.330
But, it's irritating just seeing her!

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.480
You were expecting too much from her.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:35.160
Listen, this is how you persuade people like her.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.190
You know who they are, right?

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.460
You said what you wanted to say.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:51.610
But while you were blabbering about your way,
things that could happen to your sisters in the meantime...

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.230
...try to imagine it.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.680
Mer-kun, I'm scared.

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:37.390
I think someone in this country
is laughing at us while we work hard.

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.230
Our fight isn't useless, right?

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:41.780
Next time, "The Unseen Pain".

00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:43.860
Come get us if you're not scared!
